'''Orthotrichaceae''' is the only family of [[moss]]es in the order '''Orthotrichales'''.<ref name="Goffinet 2008">{{cite book |last=Goffinet |first=B. |title=Bryophyte Biology |author2=Buck |first2=W. R. |author3=Shaw |first3=A. J. |publisher=Cambridge University Press |year=2008 |isbn=978-0-521-87225-6 |editor=Bernard Goffinet |edition=2nd |location=Cambridge |pages=55–138 |chapter=Morphology and Classification of the Bryophyta |editor2=A. Jonathan Shaw}}</ref><ref name="Goffinet & Buck 2004">{{cite journal |last=Goffinet |first=Bernard |author2=Buck |first2=William R. |year=2004 |title=Systematics of the Bryophyta (Mosses): From molecules to a revised classification |journal=Monographs in Systematic Botany |series=Molecular Systematics of Bryophytes |publisher=Missouri Botanical Garden Press |volume=98 |pages=205–239 |isbn=1-930723-38-5}}</ref> Many species in the family are [[epiphytic]].

